\p \v 20 \w On that|strong="H01931"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w*, \w HOLY|strong="H06944"\w* \w TO THE LORD|strong="H03068"\w*\f + \fr 14:20 \ft That is, \fqa the LORD\f* \w will be [inscribed]|strong="H01961"\w* \w on|strong="H05921"\w* \w the bells|strong="H04698"\w* \w of the horses|strong="H05483"\w*, \w and the cooking pots|strong="H05518"\w* \w in the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w will be|strong="H01961"\w* \w like the sprinkling bowls|strong="H04219"\w* \w before|strong="H06440"\w* \w the altar|strong="H04196"\w*. \v 21 \w Indeed, every|strong="H03605"\w* \w pot|strong="H05518"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w and Judah|strong="H03063"\w* \w will be|strong="H01961"\w* \w holy|strong="H06944"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*, \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w who sacrifice|strong="H02076"\w* \w will come|strong="H00935"\w* \w and take|strong="H03947"\w* some [pots] \w and cook|strong="H01310"\w* in them. \w And on that|strong="H01931"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w* \w there will no|strong="H03808"\w* \w longer|strong="H05750"\w* \w be|strong="H01961"\w* \w a Canaanite|strong="H03669"\w*\f + \fr 14:21 \ft Or \fqa merchant\f* \w in the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*.
